<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <!--
      Entitlements for everything inside the bundle that is signed separately: the
      Helper apps (GPU / Renderer / Plugin) and Electron Framework.framework.
      Referenced from electron-builder.yml as `mac.entitlementsInherit`; guarded by
      scripts/packaging-config.test.ts.

      Same three keys as entitlements.mac.plist, and that is correct rather than a
      copy-paste slip: the Helper processes are the ones actually running V8, so they
      need the JIT relaxations at least as much as the main bundle does. See
      entitlements.mac.plist for why each key is here and what is deliberately absent.

      Note the one key NOT carried over from the usual "inherit" template:

        com.apple.security.inherit
          App Sandbox inheritance. It is inert without com.apple.security.app-sandbox,
          which this non-store build does not set. electron-builder's own fallback for
          `entitlementsInherit` is literally the same non-sandbox template as for the
          app bundle, so omitting it matches the tool's behavior.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
  </dict>
</plist>
